<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camulogenus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 52 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Camulogenus was an elderly leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulerci">Aulerci</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> who commanded the Gallic forces around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutetia">Lutetia</a> during the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> in 52 BCE. Facing Caesar's legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Titus Labienus</a>, he burned Lutetia and its bridges and held the marshes along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a>. Labienus outmanoeuvred him, and Camulogenus was killed in the battle that followed. Caesar's Gallic War is the main source.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/camulogenus.jpg" alt="Camulogenus" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arnaud Fafournoux · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camulog%C3%A8ne_par_Eug%C3%A8ne-Louis_Lequesne._Palais_des_Beaux-Arts_de_Lille_(France).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
